  "idea": "Loom video comment threading workflow for async design reviews",
  "text": "Use timestamped video comments to point out exact layout edits and interface bugs asynchronously. Static screenshots with red markup arrows fail to capture complex animations, hover states, and responsive shifts. Designers waste hours guessing what clients meant, resulting in endless email chains and severe frustration. Dropping Loom screen recordings directly into Figma comments pairs spoken context with precise timeline timestamps. You eliminate revisions and ship polished interfaces faster.",
